  "notes": "Ichidan verb ({一段|いちだん}). {舞|ま}い{降|お}りる → {舞|ま}い{降|お}りない → {舞|ま}い{降|お}りて → {舞|ま}い{降|お}りた\n\nUSAGE:\nA compound verb combining {舞|ま}う (to dance, to flutter) and {降|お}りる (to descend). The {舞|ま}う component adds a sense of lightness and grace to the descent. Often used in literary or poetic contexts. Common subjects include birds, snow, leaves, and angels.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {鳥|とり}が{舞|ま}い{降|お}りる: a bird swoops down\n- {雪|ゆき}が{舞|ま}い{降|お}りる: snow flutters down\n- {天使|てんし}が{舞|ま}い{降|お}りる: an angel descends",
